                            <comment id="496919" author="hornc" created="Sat, 27 Jun 2026 15:26:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Forgot to post the RCA here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a latent bug in one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18812&quot; title=&quot;lnet: restrict IP addresses that socklnd listens on&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18812&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18812&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; patches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When each socklnd NI comes up, lnet_acceptor_add_socket() opens a listening socket and replaces its sk-&amp;gt;sk_data_ready with lnet_acceptor_ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;        /* Setup socket callback properly */
        lnet_acceptor_state.pta_odata = lsock-&amp;gt;liss_sock-&amp;gt;sk-&amp;gt;sk_data_ready;
        lsock-&amp;gt;liss_sock-&amp;gt;sk-&amp;gt;sk_data_ready = lnet_acceptor_ready;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;lnet_acceptor_ready() does an unconditional wake_up_interruptible()&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;        wake_up_interruptible(&amp;amp;lnet_acceptor_state.pta_waitq);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;pta_waitq is a field of the file-static lnet_acceptor_state struct, which is zero. The static initializer only sets .pta_shutdown = 1, not pta_waitq. It is only made valid by init_waitqueue_head() inside the acceptor kthread&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;static struct {
        int                     pta_shutdown;
        struct socket           *pta_sock;
        struct completion       pta_signal;
        struct net              *pta_ns;
        wait_queue_head_t       pta_waitq;
        atomic_t                pta_ready;
#ifdef HAVE_SK_DATA_READY_ONE_ARG
        void                    (*pta_odata)(struct sock *);
#else
        void                    (*pta_odata)(struct sock *, int);
#endif
} lnet_acceptor_state = {
        .pta_shutdown = 1
};

...

static int
lnet_acceptor(void *arg)
{
...
        init_waitqueue_head(&amp;amp;lnet_acceptor_state.pta_waitq);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When LNet is started, all listeners are hooked in lnet_startup_lndnets() before lnet_acceptor_start() spawns the kthread. So there is a window where the listening sockets are live and hooked but pta_waitq.head.next == NULL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An inbound TCP connection completing its 3-way handshake in that window goes tcp_v4_rcv &amp;#45;&amp;gt; tcp_child_process &amp;#45;&amp;gt; parent-&amp;gt;sk_data_ready (=lnet_acceptor_ready) -&amp;gt; wake_up_interruptible(&amp;amp;pta_waitq) and dereferences the NULL list head -&amp;gt; __wake_up_common+0x4c NULL deref in softirq -&amp;gt; panic.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
